    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and both its tests pass along with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` derived field in the standard Spring/MapStruct/OpenAPI flow the app already uses for its other derived owner fields:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `ownerSegment` property to the Owner response schema (this generates the field on `OwnerDto` at build time), documenting the `<TIER>_<AREA>` format and the four allowed values.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` for `ownerSegment` and an `ownerSegment(Owner)` method that reuses the existing derived values:\n   - **TIER** = `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel(owner) >= 3`, else `STANDARD`.\n   - **AREA** = `METRO` when the derived `locality` is a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD \u2014 checked via the existing `REGION_TIMEZONE` table whose keys are exactly those three), else `REGIONAL`.\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`STANDARD_METRO` for a known-region owner, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown city) pass, and the overall build is green.",
